{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TorusKnotTracePolynomial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TorusKnotTracePolynomial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.traceIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.traceIdentity","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L252-L275","doc":"**`P_m(h) = (q^{2m+1} + q^{−(2m+1)}) / (2·[2]_q)`**, for every `m`.\n\nThis is `docs/canonical-derivation-cheat-sheet.md` §5's identity, recorded there as\n\"sympy-exact across `m = 1..6`\". It is now a theorem over any field of characteristic\nzero, with no bound on `m`.\n\nAt a real substrate `q = e^η` the right-hand side is `cosh((2m+1)η) / (2 cosh η)`, which\nis the form the categorical Weinberg-angle statement uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_eq_chebS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_eq_chebS","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L231-L248","doc":"**The binomial sum *is* the recursion.** Two-step induction; the step is\n`chebSum_succ_succ_add` rearranged, so the additive form is used exactly once and the\nsubtraction only ever appears on the `chebS` side, where it is over a ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_succ_succ_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_succ_succ_add","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L161-L229","doc":"**`chebSum` satisfies the recursion**, in additive form.\n\nStated as `S_{m+2} + S_m = (h²+2)·S_{m+1}` rather than with a subtraction on purpose:\nthe termwise fact underneath is `choose_shift_identity`, which is an identity between\nsums of binomial coefficients in `ℕ`, and keeping it additive means no truncated\nsubtraction ever has to be reasoned about.\n\nAll three sums are first put over the common range `range (m+3)` — legitimate by\n`chebSum_eq_range`, since the extra terms vanish — after which peeling index `0`\naligns the `h²` shift with the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_eq_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum_eq_range","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L153-L159","doc":"`chebSum` may be summed over any range at least as long as its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.choose_add_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.choose_add_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L148-L151","doc":"Terms past `j = m` vanish, because `2j > m + j` there. This is what lets every\nsum in the recurrence be written over one common range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebSum","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L143-L146","doc":"The explicit binomial sum of `torus-knot-h-expansion-pattern` (PR #1125),\n`Σ_{j≤m} C(m+j, 2j)·h^{2j}` — the cheat sheet's `P_m` before its factor of `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.choose_shift_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.choose_shift_identity","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L122-L141","doc":"**The Pascal identity behind the recurrence.**\n\n`C(m+i+2, 2i+2) + C(m+i, 2i+2) = C(m+i, 2i) + 2·C(m+i+1, 2i+2)`.\n\nIndexed by `i` rather than by `j = i+1` so that every argument is a genuine natural\nnumber and no truncated subtraction appears. Three applications of Pascal's rule and\n`omega` on the resulting linear combination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_q_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_q_form","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L80-L116","doc":"**The `q`-form.** `S_m(q − q⁻¹)·(q + q⁻¹) = q^{2m+1} + q^{−(2m+1)}`.\n\nAt a real substrate `q = e^η` this reads `S_m·2cosh η = 2cosh((2m+1)η)`, i.e. the\ncheat sheet's `P_m(h₀) = cosh((2m+1)η₀)/(2 cosh η₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_succ_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_succ_succ","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L70-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebS_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chebS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chebS","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TorusKnotTracePolynomial.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The Chebyshev-type recursion underlying the `T(2,2m)` trace polynomial:\n`S₀ = 1`, `S₁ = h² + 1`, `S_{m+2} = (h² + 2)·S_{m+1} − S_m`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}